@id: scene.act_01ch_35_chains_of_light
@when: Unknown.scene_act_01ch_35_chains_of_light
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [he, keen, marithel, she, unknown]

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "Chapter 28: Chains of Light"
  - line: 3
    type: narration
    text: "The Void Spire transit ended with jarring abruptness."
  - line: 5
    type: narration
    text: "Viên and Keen materialized in a chamber of polished obsidian and gold, the transition from Umbrageous's ethereal pathways to solid reality making them both stagger."
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "The Mars Void Spire towered above them, its crystalline structure pulsing with energies that felt wrong—corrupted, constrained, bent to purposes it was never meant to serve."
  - line: 8
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Keen
    text: "\"Something's not right,\""
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "Viên's temporal patterns flared beneath his skin, warning of danger in every direction."
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber was too perfect, too prepared."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "This wasn't an arrival point—it was a trap."
  - line: 14
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Welcome, travelers.\""
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "The voice came from everywhere and nowhere, resonating through the chamber's acoustics with inhuman precision."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "From the shadows between pillars stepped figures in armor that seemed to absorb light rather than reflect it—Anunnaki soldiers, their faces hidden behind helmets that showed only glowing red eyes."
  - line: 19
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We've been expecting you,\""
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "the lead soldier continued, weapon trained on them with casual precision. \"The Queen will be pleased. The Zaryonic bloodline returns to us at last.\""
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "Viên stepped protectively in front of Keen, temporal energy gathering around his hands."
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "\"We're not here for your Queen."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "We came to warn Earth about—\""
  - line: 26
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"About the corruption spreading through the network?\""
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "The soldier's tone carried amusement. \"We know. We caused it. Every Void Spire that activates, every connection that strengthens—all of it serves our purpose.\""
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "More soldiers emerged from concealed positions, surrounding them completely."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "Their weapons hummed with energies that made Viên's teeth ache—null fields designed to suppress both magical and temporal abilities."
  - line: 32
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Keen
    text: "\"Viên,\""
  - line: 34
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Don't,\""
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "he warned quietly. \"Look at the walls.\""
  - line: 37
    type: narration
    text: "She followed his gaze and felt her heart sink."
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber walls were inscribed with geometric patterns that trapped spiritual energy, preventing phase-shifts between realms."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "They had thought of everything."
  - line: 41
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Remarkable, isn't it?\""
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "the lead soldier said. \"Designed specifically for beings like you. The Spirit Walker of the Moon Kingdom and the Temporal Guardian with the fragmented soul. Your profiles have been in our databases since before you were born.\""
  - line: 44
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"How?\""
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Keen demanded."
  - line: 47
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The Queen sees far. Plans long.\""
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "The soldier gestured, and two others moved forward with restraint devices. \"You can surrender with dignity, or we can demonstrate why resistance against the Anunnaki has always been futile.\""
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Viên felt the red curse stirring in his blood, responding to the threat with eager anticipation."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "It wanted him to fight, to unleash the corruption that would transform him into something monstrous."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "He forced it down, knowing that giving in would only serve their enemies' purposes."
  - line: 54
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"We surrender,\""
  - line: 56
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Viên!\""
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "Keen protested."
  - line: 59
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Trust me,\""
  - line: 61
    type: narration
    text: "The restraints were unlike anything they'd encountered before—not mere metal, but crystallized void energy that adapted to suppress their specific abilities."
  - line: 62
    type: narration
    text: "The moment they clicked into place, Viên felt his connection to the temporal streams severed, while Keen gasped as her spiritual abilities were locked away."
  - line: 64
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Excellent choice,\""
  - line: 65
    type: narration
    text: "the lead soldier said. \"The Queen values wisdom. She may even let you keep your minds intact when she claims you.\""
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "They were marched through corridors that seemed to twist through impossible angles."
  - line: 68
    type: narration
    text: "The Mars Void Spire's interior had been completely reconfigured, transformed from a neutral transit point into an Anunnaki stronghold."
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "Every surface bore their technology, their symbols, their absolute control."
  - line: 71
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"The corruption you're spreading,\""
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Viên said as they walked. \"Don't you realize it will destroy everything? Even you?\""
  - line: 74
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Destroy?\""
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "The soldier laughed—a sound like grinding metal. \"We're not destroying. We're preparing. The Fifth Coming requires all networks to be synchronized, all resistance to be eliminated. What you call corruption, we call evolution.\""
  - line: 77
    type: narration
    text: "They passed viewing ports that showed the Martian surface—red sands stretching to the horizon under a butterscotch sky."
  - line: 78
    type: narration
    text: "But there was activity out there, structures being built, forces gathering."
  - line: 79
    type: narration
    text: "This wasn't just an outpost."
  - line: 80
    type: narration
    text: "It was a staging ground."
  - line: 82
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Your friends on Earth,\""
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "the soldier continued conversationally. \"They scramble to unite the Giants, to gather their primitive magics. They don't understand that every move they make has been anticipated. Every alliance they forge only strengthens the network we'll soon control.\""
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "Keen tested her restraints subtly, finding no weakness."
  - line: 86
    type: narration
    text: "\"You're overconfident."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "Earth's defenders—\""
  - line: 89
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Are divided. Scattered. Fighting corruptions they don't understand with tools they can barely use.\""
  - line: 90
    type: narration
    text: "The soldier's helmet turned toward her. \"Though I admit, the one who escaped the Sun was... unexpected. We thought that prison unbreakable.\""
  - line: 92
    type: narration
    text: "They arrived at a detention block that made conventional prisons look primitive."
  - line: 93
    type: narration
    text: "Each cell was a cube of pure energy fields, designed to hold beings of immense power."
  - line: 94
    type: narration
    text: "Several were already occupied—Viên caught glimpses of other prisoners, beings from worlds he couldn't identify, all bearing the look of those who had fought and lost."
  - line: 96
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Separate cells,\""
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "the lead soldier ordered. \"The Queen's instructions were specific. The Temporal Guardian requires special containment. The Spirit Walker...\" He paused. \"She's not the primary target. Standard protocols will suffice.\""
  - line: 99
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No!\""
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "Viên struggled against his restraints as they began to separate them. \"Keen!\""
  - line: 102
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "\"It's okay,\""
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "But as they were forced into different cells, Viên felt a deep dread settling into his bones."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "The null fields in his cell were specifically calibrated to his temporal signature."
  - line: 106
    type: narration
    text: "They had been studying him, preparing for exactly this moment."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "The energy field sealed behind him with a sound like reality itself locking into place."
  - line: 109
    type: narration
    text: "Through the transparent barrier, he could see Keen being placed in a cell across the corridor."
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "Her expression was determined, defiant, but he could see the fear beneath."
  - line: 112
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Comfortable?\""
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "the lead soldier asked, standing between their cells. \"You'll have some time to adjust. The Queen is still gathering forces at the Crimson Citadel. She'll come for you when she's ready.\""
  - line: 115
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"What does she want?\""
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "Viên demanded."
  - line: 118
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"What she's always wanted. What was stolen from her eons ago.\""
  - line: 119
    type: narration
    text: "The soldier's visor turned toward him. \"The complete Zaryonic pattern. The knowledge your predecessor scattered across time and space. She's very patient, our Queen. She's waited generations for the fragments to gather themselves.\""
  - line: 121
    type: narration
    text: "The implications hit Viên like a physical blow."
  - line: 122
    type: narration
    text: "\"You mean...\""
  - line: 124
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Every fragment you've collected, every piece of your scattered soul you've recovered—all of it has been drawing you here. The Queen didn't need to hunt you. She just needed to wait for you to complete yourself. Much more efficient.\""
  - line: 126
    type: narration
    text: "With that, the soldiers departed, leaving them alone in their energy cage."
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "The silence that followed was oppressive, broken only by the subtle hum of the containment fields."
  - line: 129
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Viên?\""
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "Keen's voice carried across the corridor. \"Are you okay?\""
  - line: 132
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I'm...\""
  - line: 133
    type: narration
    text: "He touched the barrier, feeling it analyze and adapt to his temporal signature. \"I'm contained. Completely. You?\""
  - line: 135
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Same. These fields—they're learning. Every time I test them, they adapt.\""
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "Viên slumped against the back wall of his cell, the red curse pulsing angrily in his veins."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "It wanted out, wanted to transform, to break free through sheer corruption."
  - line: 139
    type: narration
    text: "But he knew that's exactly what the Anunnaki expected."
  - line: 140
    type: narration
    text: "Maybe even what they wanted."
  - line: 142
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"We need to be smart about this,\""
  - line: 144
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"So what do we do?\""
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "Before he could answer, a new presence made itself known."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "The shadows in the corridor deepened, and the temperature dropped several degrees."
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "From the darkness stepped a figure in robes of silver and shadow—clearly Anunnaki, but different from the soldiers."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Older."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "More refined."
  - line: 152
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I am Overseer Marithel,\""
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "the figure announced, voice carrying harmonics that made the cell walls vibrate. \"I've been assigned to... study you both until the Queen arrives.\""
  - line: 155
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Study?\""
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "Keen spat the word."
  - line: 158
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Observe. Document. Understand.\""
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel moved between their cells, examining them like specimens. \"The Temporal Guardian presents fascinating anomalies. The fragmentation of consciousness across temporal streams—unprecedented. And you, Spirit Walker, your connection to the lunar essence despite being off-world... intriguing.\""
  - line: 161
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We're not experiments,\""
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Viên said coldly."
  - line: 164
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Everything is an experiment to those who seek understanding.\""
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel produced a device that projected holographic displays. \"Shall we begin with your temporal signatures? The corruption in your blood is particularly interesting. It's almost as if it's waiting for something.\""
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "Viên felt the red curse stir again, responding to being mentioned."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "\"I won't help you understand anything.\""
  - line: 170
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Marithel
    text: "\"You already are,\""
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer began taking readings, the device in their hands recording information Viên couldn't begin to understand."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "But what disturbed him most was how the red curse seemed to recognize the scanning, almost welcoming it."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "Time passed strangely in the cells."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "Without windows, without natural light, it was impossible to tell if hours or days were passing."
  - line: 177
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel came and went, sometimes with new devices, sometimes with questions that probed at the edges of their memories and abilities."
  - line: 179
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Marithel
    text: "\"The network corruption,\""
  - line: 181
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It's killing worlds,\""
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "Keen protested."
  - line: 184
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"It's elevating them. Those that survive will be stronger. Those that don't...\""
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "A shrug. \"Evolution has always been cruel.\""
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "It was during their third or fourth session—time had become meaningless—that everything changed."
  - line: 188
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel was in the middle of explaining some aspect of the corruption's propagation when alarms began blaring throughout the facility."
  - line: 190
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"What—\""
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "the Overseer began, then their head snapped toward the entrance. \"Impossible. The perimeter defenses...\""
  - line: 193
    type: narration
    text: "The lights flickered."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "The energy fields of their cells wavered for just a moment—not enough to escape, but enough to show they weren't infallible."
  - line: 196
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Security breach in sections 7 through 12,\""
  - line: 197
    type: narration
    text: "an automated voice announced. \"Intruder classification: Unknown. Threat level: Severe.\""
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel hurried from the detention block, leaving them alone."
  - line: 200
    type: narration
    text: "Whatever was happening had clearly caught the Anunnaki by surprise."
  - line: 202
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Keen
    text: "\"Viên,\""
  - line: 204
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Yes. Something disrupted them. Something the Anunnaki didn't expect.\""
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "More alarms joined the first, creating a cacophony of warnings."
  - line: 207
    type: narration
    text: "The lights flickered again, longer this time."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "In the distance, they could hear the sounds of combat—energy weapons discharge, explosions, and something else."
  - line: 209
    type: narration
    text: "Something that sounded like reality itself tearing."
  - line: 211
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Shadow-walking,\""
  - line: 212
    type: narration
    text: "Keen breathed. \"Someone's shadow-walking through their defenses.\""
  - line: 214
    type: narration
    text: "Hope flared in Viên's chest."
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "Could it be?"
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "Had someone come for them?"
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "The combat sounds grew closer."
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "The energy fields flickered more frequently now, the facility's power grid clearly under strain."
  - line: 220
    type: narration
    text: "Then, from the shadows themselves, a figure emerged."
  - line: 222
    type: narration
    text: "Rongtai stumbled into the detention block, her shadow-light magic flickering unstably around her form."
  - line: 223
    type: narration
    text: "She looked exhausted, pushed beyond her limits, but determination burned in her eyes."
  - line: 225
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Rongtai!\""
  - line: 226
    type: narration
    text: "Keen cried out."
  - line: 228
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"No time,\""
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "the Weaver gasped, already moving to Keen's cell. \"The amplifier burned out. I can't maintain this for long. The shadows here—they're different. Wrong.\""
  - line: 231
    type: narration
    text: "She pressed her hands against Keen's containment field, shadow-light energy pouring into the barrier."
  - line: 232
    type: narration
    text: "The field resisted, adapted, but Rongtai's power was unlike anything it had been designed for."
  - line: 233
    type: narration
    text: "Slowly, painfully, the barrier began to fail."
  - line: 235
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Keen
    text: "\"What about Viên?\""
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "Rongtai looked at Viên's cell, exhaustion clear on her face."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "\"I can't."
  - line: 239
    type: narration
    text: "Not enough power left."
  - line: 240
    type: narration
    text: "The fields—they're too strong.\""
  - line: 242
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Go,\""
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "Viên said immediately. \"Get Keen out of here.\""
  - line: 245
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Viên, no!\""
  - line: 246
    type: narration
    text: "Keen protested."
  - line: 248
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "\"Listen to me,\""
  - line: 250
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I won't leave you!\""
  - line: 252
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"You have to.\""
  - line: 253
    type: narration
    text: "He pressed his hand against the barrier, and she mirrored the gesture from outside. \"Rongtai can't free us both. And Earth needs to know.\""
  - line: 255
    type: narration
    text: "Tears streamed down Keen's face, but she nodded."
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "The footsteps were getting closer—Anunnaki reinforcements responding to the breach."
  - line: 258
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"We'll come back for you,\""
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "she promised. \"All of us. Together.\""
  - line: 261
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"I know.\""
  - line: 262
    type: narration
    text: "He managed a smile, though the red curse was raging inside him at being left behind. \"Now go. Before they—\""
  - line: 264
    type: narration
    text: "Anunnaki soldiers burst into the detention block, weapons already firing."
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "Rongtai grabbed Keen, shadow-light erupting around them both."
  - line: 266
    type: narration
    text: "The last thing Viên saw was Keen's tearful face as the shadows swallowed them, carrying them away from the Mars Void Spire."
  - line: 268
    type: narration
    text: "The soldiers rushed past his cell in pursuit, but Viên knew they were already too late."
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "Rongtai's shadow-walking was unlike anything else—once she had someone in the shadow realm, tracking them was nearly impossible."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel returned minutes later, clearly agitated."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "\"The Spirit Walker escaped."
  - line: 273
    type: narration
    text: "How... interesting.\""
  - line: 275
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"She'll warn Earth,\""
  - line: 276
    type: narration
    text: "Viên said, allowing himself a moment of satisfaction. \"Your plans—\""
  - line: 278
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Are unaffected.\""
  - line: 279
    type: narration
    text: "Marithel's composure returned. \"We have what we really wanted. You. The Queen will be most pleased to learn her primary target is secured.\""
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "The Overseer studied him with renewed interest."
  - line: 282
    type: narration
    text: "\"In fact, this works better."
  - line: 283
    type: narration
    text: "Your emotional state, the isolation, the growing desperation—all of it will make the corruption's emergence that much more powerful when it finally manifests.\""
  - line: 285
    type: narration
    text: "Viên felt the red curse pulse in agreement, and for the first time since their capture, true fear settled into his heart."
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "Not of the Anunnaki, not of imprisonment, but of what he carried inside himself."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "What would emerge when the Queen finally came to claim her prize."
  - line: 289
    type: narration
    text: "In the darkness of his cell, alone now without even Keen's presence across the corridor, Viên prepared himself for whatever came next."
  - line: 290
    type: narration
    text: "The fragments of his temporal soul pulsed within him, each one making the curse stronger, making the transformation more inevitable."
  - line: 292
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere in the Martian desert, Keen and Rongtai were fleeing toward safety."
  - line: 293
    type: narration
    text: "Somewhere on Earth, their friends continued their quest, unaware of what had transpired."
  - line: 294
    type: narration
    text: "And somewhere in the depths of space, the Queen turned her attention toward Mars, toward the prize she had waited eons to claim."
  - line: 296
    type: narration
    text: "The game was entering its final phase, and Viên found himself a captive piece on a board whose true scope he was only beginning to understand."
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "But even pawns could sometimes change the course of the game."
  - line: 299
    type: narration
    text: "He just had to survive long enough to find out how."

=inferred:
  actions:
    - {line: 206, action: creation, confidence: 0.90}

=narrative:
  "act_01ch_35_chains_of_light - 299 segments"
  blank: 96
  dialogue: 55
  narration: 148